# Shadowing in a nested scope allowed

Verifies a nested block may declare a name that already exists in an enclosing
scope. The inner binding shadows the outer one and may have a different type;
after the block the outer binding is visible again.

>>> source
let x: int = 10

{
    let x: string = "hello"
    print(x)
}

print(x)

<<< stdout
hello
10

<<< stderr
